From 602963fab7ff7d1e3b9b7d18e12e877d2a4d3b5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:24:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: lahaina: Use the 6.12 WALT and memlat nodes on yupik

The 6.12 kernel runs the WALT module, which keeps its tunables under
/proc/sys/walt and takes per task values as "pid value" pairs, and it
scales LLCC and DDR through bus_dcvs. The yupik resources still pointed
at the 5.4 nodes, so per task boost, low latency and wake up idle, the
LLCC bandwidth and the memlat ceilings all failed to apply, as did the
DDR and L3 floors the scroll, launch and frame hints asked for.

Map those resources to the nodes kalama uses, with the yupik bwmon
addresses, and mark the ones the kernel no longer has unsupported. The
per cluster migrate pair stays on /proc/sys/kernel/%s, which WALT keeps
as a compat table. In the yupik hints, ask the DDR bwmon for 681 MHz
while scrolling as kalama does, and drop the old DDR, L3 and
sched_prefer_spread requests.
